 it to verify a statement signed by it. For a member DID reached over TSP, the TSP VID is the DID itself."},"GrantView":{"title":"GrantView","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["statement","state","scope","expiresAt"],"description":"The mediator\'s view of one stored grant, as messaging/mux/list and messaging/mux/update return it: the grant statement verbatim, with the state and the effective scope and expiry beside it.","properties":{"statement":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GrantStatement","description":"The grant statement exactly as the member signed it and the mediator stored it, proof included, so either party can re-verify it."},"state":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GrantState"},"scope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxScope","description":"The effective scope: the signed scope, or the narrower one messaging/mux/update set."},"expiresAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"The effective expiry: the signed `exp` rendered as RFC 3339, or the earlier one messaging/mux/update set."},"narrowed":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when messaging/mux/update narrowed the effective scope or expiry below what the statement signs."},"attachedNow":{"type":"boolean","description":"Principal view only: whether the member is attached through this grant to the connection that carried the list request."}}},"GrantState":{"title":"GrantState","type":"string","enum":["active","suspended","staleKey","expired","epochRevoked"],"description":"A stored grant\'s state. `active`: valid; the member is attached whenever the principal is connected. `suspended`: the member DID proved control with a key that signed none of its active grants (the unknown-key rule); terminal — the grant cannot be resumed and must be recreated by a fresh member signature. `staleKey`: the key that signed the grant is no longer in the member DID\'s current authentication relationship; terminal — it does not become active again if the key reappears. `expired`: an active grant past its effective expiry; computed when read, never stored. `epochRevoked`: the member DID advanced its epoch with messaging/mux/revoke-all. A grant revoked with messaging/mux/revoke has no state: it is deleted. A dead grant (every state but `active`) stays listable for the mediator\'s retention window after its effective expiry, then is pruned."},"GrantStatement":{"title":"GrantStatement","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["type","issuer","audience","grantId","principal","scope","epoch","iat","exp","proof"],"description":"A member DID\'s standing statement that the named principal may carry its traffic at this mediator, on any connection, until `exp`, within `scope`, under the member\'s current `epoch`. Signed by the member with an embedded Data Integrity proof whose purpose is `authentication`, and stored verbatim by the mediator as the only evidence of the delegation.","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"muxGrant","description":"Always `muxGrant`; names the statement kind, so a statement of one kind is never accepted as another."},"issuer":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxDid","description":"The member DID: the signer, and the DID the statement concerns."},"audience":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxDid","description":"The mediator\'s DID. A statement names exactly one mediator and is refused by every other."},"grantId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GrantId"},"principal":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxDid","description":"The principal DID that may carry the member\'s traffic. MUST differ from `issuer`."},"scope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/StatementScope"},"epoch":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The member DID\'s current epoch at the mediator. Only messaging/mux/revoke-all advances it."},"iat":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"JWT NumericDate (RFC 7519 §2), whole seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z UTC: when the statement was signed. MUST NOT be more than 60 seconds in the mediator\'s future."},"exp":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"JWT NumericDate (RFC 7519 §2): when the statement stops being accepted. REQUIRED; MUST be after `iat` and in the future."},"proof":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxDataIntegrityProof"}}},"MuxDataIntegrityProof":{"title":"MuxDataIntegrityProof","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["type","cryptosuite","verificationMethod","proofPurpose","proofValue"],"description":"The W3C Data Integrity proof embedded in a mux statement, made by the member DID: the format and verifier Trust Tasks already use for document proofs (SPEC §4.7). The proof covers the whole statement except `proof` itself, as the cryptosuite defines. Closed: a member Data Integrity defines but this list omits is refused.","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"DataIntegrityProof"},"cryptosuite":{"type":"string","enum":["eddsa-jcs-2022","eddsa-rdfc-2022"],"description":"The W3C Data Integrity EdDSA cryptosuite used."},"verificationMethod":{"type":"string","minLength":5,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^did:\\\\S+#\\\\S+\$","description":"The DID URL of the verification method that signed. MUST be controlled by the statement\'s `issuer` and listed in that DID\'s current `authentication` relationship."},"proofPurpose":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"MUST be `authentication`. Any other value is refused with `messaging/mux:proofPurposeInvalid` — a proof made for another relationship (an `assertionMethod` credential signature, say) is never accepted as control of the DID."},"created":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"OPTIONAL: when the proof was made, as Data Integrity defines it. Covered by the proof; the statement\'s own `iat` is what the mediator checks."},"proofValue":{"type":"string","minLength":2,"maxLength":4096,"pattern":"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]+\$","description":"The multibase (base58btc) signature."}}},"StatementScope":{"title":"StatementScope","type":"array","maxItems":16,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/MuxScopeValue"},"description":"The scope a member DID signs into a statement: a JSON array of MuxScopeValue, compared as a set — order is not significant and a repeated value collapses. It MUST NOT be empty; an empty signed scope is refused with the task\'s `emptyScope` code, never read as \\"all\\". Unlike MuxScope, emptiness is not a schema failure here, so that the refusal is reported per statement rather than failing the whole batch."},"GrantId":{"title":"GrantId","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]+\$","description":"A grant\'s identifier, chosen by the member DID\'s signer and carried in its grant statement; a UUID is RECOMMENDED. A mediator refuses a grant whose identifier is already on the member DID\'s record."},"MuxRole":{"title":"MuxRole","type":"string","enum":["principal","member"],"description":"The side of a delegation a requester acts as. `principal`: the DID that authenticated the connection and to which members\' traffic is delegated. `member`: a DID whose traffic is delegated."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: false,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: false,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
